(synth/sine (frequency) {detune 0 octave 0}) "A sine wave at frequency in Hz, a number or a sound that changes it, or at the pitch of the note playing when frequency is left out. :detune shifts it by cents and :octave by octaves."
(synth/saw (frequency) {detune 0 octave 0}) "A sawtooth wave, bright and buzzy, at frequency or the note's pitch; :detune in cents and :octave as for synth/sine."
(synth/triangle (frequency) {detune 0 octave 0}) "A triangle wave, soft and hollow, at frequency or the note's pitch; :detune in cents and :octave as for synth/sine."
(synth/square (frequency) {detune 0 octave 0 width 0.5}) "A pulse wave at frequency or the note's pitch, high for :width of each cycle, a number or a sound from 0 to 1; 0.5 is a square."
(synth/noise (color)) "Noise: :white, :pink, which is softer at the top, or :brown, a low rumble."
(synth/pitch) "The frequency in Hz of the note playing, as oscillators use when given no frequency."
(synth/gate) "1 while the note is held and 0 once it is let go."
(synth/velocity) "How hard the note was played, from 0 to 1. Notes are already as loud as their velocity; use this to change their tone too."
(synth/input) "What reaches a track's :effects or synth/process: the mixed voices or the sample's sound."
(synth/control name default {low nil high nil}) "A value that can change while the sound plays, called name, such as :cutoff, starting at default. synth/set, sliders in the bellow workbench and automations move it between :low and :high, smoothly."
(synth/lfo rate low high {wave :sine}) "A slow wave, rate times a second, swinging between low and high, for vibrato, tremolo or a filter that breathes. :wave is :sine, :triangle, :saw or :square."
(synth/range sound low high) "Sound moved from -1 to 1 into low to high."
(synth/sampler sample {root nil loop false start 0}) "Plays sample from :start seconds. With :root, a note such as :c4, notes play it faster or slower to sound at their pitch; :loop true plays it again and again while the note is held."
(synth/grains sample {size 0.12 density 20 position 0.5 spread 0.05 root nil}) "A cloud of short overlapping grains read from sample: :density grains a second, each :size seconds long, from :position, 0 for its start and 1 for its end, a number or a sound that moves through it, give or take :spread. With :root, notes pitch the grains as synth/sampler does."
(synth/mix sound & more) "The sounds added together. Numbers among them add a fixed amount, as for a frequency that wobbles around a center."
(synth/mul sound & more) "The sounds multiplied together sample by sample, as for tremolo, ring modulation or an amount that follows another sound."
(synth/gain sound amount) "Sound made louder or softer by amount, a number or a sound. Given a sample, a new sample scaled by amount."
(synth/envelope sound {attack 0.01 decay 0.2 sustain 0.8 release 0.3}) "Shapes sound's loudness over each note: it rises over :attack seconds, falls over :decay to :sustain, from 0 to 1, while the note is held, and fades over :release once it is let go."
(synth/lowpass sound cutoff {resonance 0}) "Sound with what is above cutoff Hz taken away, darker as cutoff falls; :resonance from 0 to 1 rings at the cutoff. cutoff may be a sound."
(synth/highpass sound cutoff {resonance 0}) "Sound with what is below cutoff Hz taken away, thinner as cutoff rises."
(synth/bandpass sound cutoff {resonance 0}) "Only the part of sound around cutoff Hz, narrower with more :resonance, as for vowels or a telephone."
(synth/notch sound cutoff {resonance 0}) "Sound with the part around cutoff Hz taken away."
(synth/drive sound amount) "Sound pushed into warm distortion, from 0 for clean to 1 for fuzz."
(synth/fold sound amount) "Sound folded back on itself each time it passes the top or bottom, from 0 for clean to 1 for harsh, metallic overtones, harsher than synth/drive."
(synth/crush sound {bits 8 rate nil}) "Sound broken into steps of :bits, from 1 for harsh to 16 for nearly clean, and held at :rate samples a second when given, for gritty, digital tones. Both may be sounds."
(synth/compress sound {threshold 0.25 ratio 4 attack 0.005 release 0.15 key nil}) "Sound kept from growing past :threshold, what rises above it turned down :ratio times, reacting within :attack seconds and letting go over :release. With :key, a track's name such as :kick, it listens to that track instead, so the sound ducks under it and pumps."
(synth/vowel sound vowel) "Sound shaped like a voice singing vowel: :a, :e, :i, :o or :u, or a number or a sound from 0, a, to 4, u, that glides through them in that order."
(synth/pan sound position) "Sound placed from -1, left, through 0, the middle, to 1, right. position may be a sound that moves it."
(synth/delay sound seconds {feedback 0.35 mix 0.3 cross false}) "Echoes of sound every seconds, each :feedback as loud as the one before, :mix of them blended with the sound itself; :cross true bounces them between left and right."
(synth/reverb sound {size 0.8 damping 0.3 mix 0.35}) "Sound in a room: :size from 0, a small room, to 1, a hall whose tail lasts many seconds, :damping softening the tail's top, and :mix of the room blended with the sound."
(synth/chorus sound {rate 0.5 depth 0.004 mix 0.4}) "Sound thickened by slightly delayed copies that drift :rate times a second by up to :depth seconds, wider on the left and right."
(synth/notes text {velocity 0.8}) "A pattern of notes such as \"a4 . c5 e5 | d5 _ _ c5\": bars split by |, each split evenly by its slots, a note name, _ holding the note before and . a silence."
(synth/chords text {octave 3 velocity 0.6}) "A pattern of chords such as \"Dm9 _ | Bbmaj7 _ | F _ | C/E _\" with their roots in :octave: major, m, 5, 6, m6, 7, maj7, m7, mmaj7, 9, maj9, m9, add9, madd9, 11, m11, 13, maj13, sus2, sus4, dim and aug, with /bass for a bass note below."
(synth/beats text {note :c4 velocity 0.7}) "A pattern of hits such as \"X . x . | x . . x\": x a hit at :velocity, X an accent, . a silence, all at :note."
(synth/track name sound pattern {effects nil gain 1}) "A track called name playing pattern with sound, one voice for each note. :effects is a sound built on synth/input that the track's mixed voices pass through once, such as (synth/reverb (synth/input)), and :gain sets its loudness."
(synth/song & parts) "A song of the tracks among parts, which may also give :tempo, 120 beats a minute unless given, :meter, 4 beats a bar, :bars, its length when it is not as long as its longest pattern, and :automate, a map of controls to points such as {swell: [[0 0] [8 1]]} that moves them bar by bar. Each track's pattern repeats as it ends."
(synth/frequency note) "The frequency in Hz of note, such as :a4 for 440, or a MIDI number such as 69."
(synth/load path) "Reads a sound file, WAV, FLAC, MP3 or Ogg Vorbis, as a stereo sample."
(synth/render thing {seconds nil bars nil note :c4 velocity 0.8}) "Plays thing without a speaker and gives what it sounded like as a sample: a sound held :seconds, 1 unless given, at :note and :velocity and then let go until it is quiet, or a song for :bars, its length unless given, with its tails. A sample stays as it is."
(synth/save thing path {seconds nil bars nil note :c4 velocity 0.8}) "Renders thing as synth/render does and writes it to path as a 16-bit stereo WAV file, returning path."
(synth/slice sample from (to)) "The part of sample from from seconds to to seconds, or to its end."
(synth/reverse sample) "Sample backwards, as for swells that grow into a note."
(synth/resample sample ratio) "Sample played ratio times as fast: 2 is an octave higher and half as long, 0.5 an octave lower and twice as long."
(synth/fade sample {in 0 out 0}) "Sample fading in over :in seconds and out over :out seconds."
(synth/normalize sample {peak 1}) "Sample made as loud as can be with its loudest point at :peak."
(synth/join sample & more) "The samples one after another."
(synth/layer sample & more) "The samples played together, as long as the longest."
(synth/process sample effects {tail 2}) "Sample passed through effects, a sound built on synth/input, with :tail seconds more for echoes and rooms to ring out."
(synth/info sample) "A map of sample's :seconds, :rate, :peak and :rms loudness."
